From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 18:27:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-13: all-pages sweep + its two fixes, right-click
 menu, F7, fonts, form resize (0.13.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

User 20260929: "一輪一輪 持續做下去 不要等".

Found by the new all-pages sweep (real VS Code, all 80 pages of web\page;
no page had a JS error):
- fix: a page reloading in the background restored its selection and took the
  tree and the properties panel away from the page on screen. A hidden page's
  selection is now kept and shown when that page becomes active again
- fix: Setup.BinSelNormal.html is only location.replace('Setup.BinSel.html'),
  which navigated the designer away from itself. Forwarding pages (empty body +
  location.replace / href = / meta refresh) now show a notice and a button to
  open the target in the designer

WPF operations:
- right-click on the design surface selects (unless already selected) and opens
  the designer menu (webview/context): view code, HTML source, DFM definition,
  select parent, find, Align submenu, overview, mode; the page never sees it
- F7 = view code (the default event), like WPF
- properties: Font.Name, Font.Bold, Font.Italic
- the form itself resizes (Width/Height, e/s/se handles, Ctrl+arrows) but never
  moves, like a WPF Window
- fix: a pending arrow-key nudge flushed after the selection moved on took the
  selection back
- "HT9045: 設計檢視使用說明" opens the README

Tests: lib 87 / probe 2 pages x 27 (right-click, select parent, form resize,
fonts, both-side anchoring) / fake vscode 54 + panels 10 / real VS Code 54 and
the re-run of the two failing pages; vscode_it.ps1 -AllPages for the sweep.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
